Uniform title: Śivotsavacaṇḍotsavabhaktotsavasahita
Manuscript : IFP manuscript bundle RE32412
Description: RE32412 - Śivotsava–Caṇḍotsava–Bhaktotsavasahita. The bundle is a detailed ritual compendium focusing on major Śaiva festival observations. The Śiva-mahotsavavidhi section outlines procedures for grand temple festivals, including chapters on Vṛṣayāgakrama, Utsavapaddhati, Dhvajārohaṇavidhi, Avarohaṇavidhi, Yānakramavidhi, Balilakṣaṇam, Rathārohaṇam, Kṛṣṇagandhavidhi and Cūrṇotsavavidhi. It further encompasses specialized ritual manuals such as Caṇḍotsavavidhi, Ācāryotsavavidhi, Devotsavam, Bhaktotsavavidhi, and Kṣetrapālavidhi, offering a comprehensive picture of the diverse ritual culture surrounding Śaiva celebrations and processional worship.The manuscript comprises 102 folios, each measuring 140 mm × 15 mm, written in 6 lines per folio. The text is in Sanskrit, transmitted in the traditional Grantha script. Despite the compact format, it preserves a rich variety of festival rituals, making it a significant resource for understanding the performative and communal dimensions of Śaiva temple culture.
