aparedyu(dyuḥ) snānādikaṃ kṛtvā – (l.6) sakalīkaraṇaṃ kṛtvā sāmānyārghyaṃ saṅkalpya – bhūtaśuddhi-antaryajanādikaṃ sarvaṃ vidhāya – gandhādyai paṭaṃ kumbhaṃ yathākrameṇābhyarcya (p.71b, f66a, l.1) .....nābhau vṛṣabhaṃ saṃpūjya । vahnau vṛṣabhaṃ saṃpūjya – samidājyena caruṇā aṣṭottaraśataṃ kṛtvā – vṛṣabhamūlamantreṇa pūrṇāṃ datvā nirudhyā(dhya) – paścāt prāsādasya (l.2) aratā gomayālepitakṣetramaṇṭape maṇṭapasaṃskārādikaṃ kṛtvā tatpuruṣeṇa prokṣya – tataḥ sthaṇḍilatrayaṃ kṛtvā - (l.3) ....... vilikhyā(khya) paricārakamāhūyā(ya) । astreṇa prokṣya soṣṇīṣauttarīyaṃ ca dhārayitvā – vṛṣapaṭasamīpaṃ gatvā – (l.4) vījasthālayamiti uddhṛtya – kumbhādisahitam astradevaṃ ca somāskandasahitaṃ sarva(rvā)todyasamā grāmapradakṣiṇaṃ kṛtvā śaṅkhadundubhinirghoṣai (l.5) brāhmaṇaghoṣasaha ālayaṃ praviśya tatpaṭaṃ hṛdayena sthaṇḍilopari nidhāya – astrarājaekena sthaṇḍile tadagre nidhā.... (l.6)vidyeśvarāvṛtavṛṣabhakumbham ekasthaṇḍile tadagre nidhāya । tatra puṇyāhaṃ vācayitvā (p.72a, l.1) vṛṣabhakumbhajalena snāpayitvā – dhvajasramadhye – vṛṣabhabījaṃ vinyasya – vidyeśvaraghaṭān vṛṣabhagāyatrimantreṇa prokṣya - pañcagavya(l.2)pañcāmṛtādinā vṛṣabhā(bhaṃ) ca snāpya – gandhapuṣpādinābhyarcya tadagre sthaṇḍilam aṣṭadroṇaśālibhiḥ vidhāyā(ya) navakumbhān ādāyā(ya) (l.3) sakūrcasāpidhānasahiraṇyavastrādyairalaṅkṛtyā(tya) vidyeśvarādyāvṛtaḥ vṛṣabhadevatā-māvāhya – ukṣādi sva sva mantrai(l.4)rāvāhya – gandhādyairarcanā । havirnivedya japāntaṃ saṃpūjya । tatkumbhajalena śūlamastra-rāja(jaṃ) saṃsnāpyālaṅkṛtvābhyarcya (l.5) nivedya vṛṣabhagāyatri(tra)yadhvajaṃ cābhyarcya – ga(gu)ladadhyānnaṃ mudgānnaṃ nivedya – astrarājasya kautukaṃ hṛdayena dāpayet (p.72b, l.1) bṛhatsāmeti pūrṇāṃ datvā – bhaktānāṃ paricārakānāṃ dāpayet – tataḥ dhvajadaṇḍamalaṅkṛtya – mālābharaṇavastrādikaṃ datvā vṛṣabhagāyatrimantreṇa (l.2) ghaṇṭāṃ badhnīyāt – dhvajadaṇḍasya anyadaṇḍaṃ rathe samāropya – ālayāgre ṇa?yet । ācāryo'grataḥ vṛṣato yajamānaḥ brāhmādi(l.3)īśānaparyantaṃ digpālānāṃ balirvidadhyāt – tataḥ bhaktajanaiḥ sārdhaṃ grāmapradakṣiṇaṃ kṛtvā – ālayaṃ praveśayet – daṇḍasthāne (l.4) ānīyya sarva(rvā)todyasamāyuktaṃ maṅgalāṅkurasaṃyutam – pūrṇakumbhasā(sa)hitaṃ nānādikdīpayuktaṃ caturdikṣu gītanṛttaśobhitam - (l.5) dhvajasthāne puṇyāhaṃ vācayitvā – vedikā toyenābhyukṣya – ādhāraśaktyādiśaktyantamāsanā vedikābhyarcya – daṇḍe sadāśivaṃ dhyātvā – āvāhyābhyarcya skandeṣu somasūryāgni...padaṇḍe – anilaṃ ca rajjustakṣādhidevatyā (p.73a, l.1) paṭeścā(śca) vāyudevatāṃ dhvaje vṛṣabhadevatāmāvāhya – krameṇābhyarcya – mudgānnaṃ pāyasānnaṃ vṛṣabhāya nivedya tāmbūlādi datvā – (l.2) bhaktānāṃ janebhyo tāmbūlaṃ datvā dhūpadīpaṃ datvā tataḥ dhvajaṃ samuddhṛtya rajjunā bandhayet – śivaṃ vijñāpya – sumuhūrte sulagne (l.3) vādyaghoṣasamanvitam uttamam utsavaṃ kriyate iti deśikaḥ । vṛṣabhamūlena sthitvā – anyā paricāraka-proktyaṃ(proktam) ārohaṇārthaṃ (l.4) svayaṃ ca – ādau spṛṣṭvā – śi(śī)ghramāropayet – daṇḍaṃ samarpya – krameṇa mūlarajjuṃ bandhayet – prabhṛtīrthāntaṃ (l.5) vṛṣabhadevatā ārohāvasānakālaparyanta-trikālaṃ dvikālam ekakālaṃ va(vā) pūjayet । evaṃ pra...(tya)hamabhyarcya mudgānnaṃ gulasahitaṃ (p.73b, l.1) dāpayet । paścāt vṛṣabhāya namaḥ । iti japam aṣṭottaraśataṃ nivedya – aṅgamantreṇa daśāṃśaśataṃ japet – prā? hṛdayāya namaḥ । hriṃ(hrīṃ) śirase namaḥ । (l.2) oṃ prarūṃ śikhāya namaḥ । oṃ vraiṃ kavacāya namaḥ । oṃ vrauṃ netrebhyo namaḥ । oṃ vruḥ astrāya namaḥ iti ne(nai)...(ve)dya paścāt kuṇḍāntikaṃ gatvā – samidbhiḥ (l.3) ājyenānnena aṣṭottaraśataṃ hutvā – vṛṣabhamūlamantreṇa pūrṇāṃ datvā – vṛṣabhāgniṃ visarjayet – caturdikṣu । śuddha-nitta(narta)nam । kāryā (l.4) iti dhvajārohaṇavidhiḥ ॥ vātule
tatpiṇḍaṃ prāśayennāri(rī) । atriputramāpnuyāt – vyādhighnaṃ sarvadoṣaghnam । vṛṣo'(l.5)bhīṣṭaṃ śikhidhvajā – śrīmanmṛgendre ।
(yānakramavidhiḥ)
	yatraitat kriyate rāṣṭre dhvajaṣṭiniveśanaṃ tatra trikālamabhyaśrā(rcya) tatra lakṣmī vācakṛtsvapi । (l.6) nopasargā-dayastatrāno parāganavibhramaṃ pūrvoktavat vidhisamalaṅkṛtya rathe raṅge kheṭake (p.74a, l.1) śibikādau vā nānālaṅkārapuṣpa-prabhāsamāyutam । devaśaktyāsahitamūlasthāne – samānīyya – āvāhyā(hya) dhūpadīpau datvā puṣpāñjalinābhyarcya (l.2) śāntyādibhaktāntaberasahitaṃ pradakṣiṇamupakramet agrato nānālaṅkārasahitaṃ beryādivādyasahitaṃ nani? vināyakasubrahmaṇyau (l.3) madhye devyā saha soma(mā)skandamagrato pṛṣṭhato ha(vi)bhaktabherāścā(śca) tatpaścāt caṇḍeśvaraṃ ca deśikaḥ savyabhāge sthitvā (l.4) mūlaṃ aghoraṃ vā japet – agrato nṛpaḥ pṛṣṭhato yajamānaḥ devadāsyanṛttakivaṃśagāyakamuravakamahāśaivāḥ (l.5) pṛṣṭhato vedādighoṣaiyu(ryu)ktaḥ tatpaścāt cāturvarṇābhā candramaṇḍalaṃ va maheśvarānugacchantaḥ aśvamedhaphalaṃ labhet – evaṃ (p.74b, l.1) santoṣya prathameha prātaḥ raṅgaṃ rātrau haṃsam । dvitīyyehani – sūryaḥ rātrau candramaṇḍalam । tri(tṛ)tīyyehani – bhūtaḥ rātrau śikharayukta(l.2)rāvaṇayantraṃ caturthe'hani – śibikā rātrau nāgayantram । pañcamehi(ha)ni kheṭakam । rātrau vṛṣabham । pradakṣa(kṣi)mānantaram । pariveṣaṇaṃ (l.3) kuryāt । udyānādiṣvakaṇe kaṇe vedastuti । śrutivīṇāveṇugāyaka-nṛttakarudragaṇikāsahitaṃ phalādyupahāraistāmbūlādibhiśca pade pade devaṃ santoṣyālayaṃ praviśya – ṣaṣṭhe'hani – śibikāyāṃ kheṭake vā samāropya cūrṇotsavaṃ (l.4) vakṣyamāṇavat kṛtvā – kuṅkumakusumbhaharidrādijaleśca devān saṃpūjya – prokṣyā(kṣya) kuṅkumapaṅkairastreṇa devamālipya - (l.5) sarvān prokṣayet rātrau gajabhi – saptame ratham aṣṭame aśvāropaṇaṃ kṛtvā – yānakāle'śvārūḍā(ḍhā) kundādyāyudhayuktakeṭakayukta(p.75a, l.1)sarvālaṅkārasahitarudragaṇikaparito vrajeyuḥ । atrāntare – pa? duṣṭanigrahaśiṣṭaparipālanaṃ kṛtvā – sakaladharmādharmāśrāvayo (l.2) a? paścādālayaṃ praviśet – navāhe puruṣayantrayaktāndolikāsakheṭake – rātrau kṛṣṇagandhaṃ daśame'hi(ha)ni siṃhāsane (l.3) devaṃ samāropya – purādikaṃ pradakṣiṇīkṛtyā(tya) harmyāgre dhvajāgre vā vikṛtānna paribhrāmya – taccatuṣpathe prakṣipet - (l.4) nīrāñjanapaṭadīpaṃ datvā śailādi nandivināyakaścaṇḍeśvaraḥ sapradakṣiṇīkṛtyālayaṃ haraṇārthaṃ nālikereṣu (l.5) sāramudgasūpatatkālocitaphalāni nivedyā(dya) brāhmaṇān gandhapuṣpairalaṅkṛtyā(tya) dīnāndhakṛpaṇādīn brāhmaṇā(ṇān) (l.6) bhojayet athavānyaprakāreṇa kuryāditi yānakramavidhiḥ ॥
(yāgaśālapūjā -)
	guruḥ snānādikaṃ kṛtvā । pādau prakṣālyā(lya) । ācamya । yāga(p.75b, l.1)śālāyāṃ vighneśvarapūjādipuṇyāhaṃ kṛtvā – saṃprokṣyā(kṣya) – sakalīkaraṇadvārapūjābhūtaśuddhiantaryāgādi kṛtvā dvārapūjādikalaśā(l.2)rādhanaṃ pūrvavat kṛtvā naivedyādikaṃ kṛtvā – paścāt kuṇḍasamīpaṃ gatvā darpaṇadīpanāntaṃ vidhāyā(ya) mūlamantreṇā(l.3)ṣṭottaraśataṃ samidhānnājyaiḥ hutvā lājādinavadhānyai(yaiḥ)-pañcabrahmaṣaḍaṅgaiśca aṣṭottaraśataṃ hṛtvā pūrṇāṃ datvā (l.4) naivedyādibhiḥ saṃpūjyāstreśaṃ samastavighnanivāraṇāya kalpitatriśūlaṃ pūjādyairalaṅkṛtya saṃpūjya naivedyādibhiḥ saṃpūjya (l.5) agnibījena aṣṭottaraśataṃ hutvā vṛṣakāyatryā tanmūlamantreṇa hutvā – pūrṇāṃ dadyāt – antarbali bahirbaliṃ ca kṛtvā vṛṣau tailādi(p.76a, l.1)gandhadravyaiḥ saṃpūjyālaṅkṛtya naivedyādi kṛtvā pūrṇāṃ dadyāt dhvajadaṇḍamūle padmaṃ tailādibhiḥ saṃpūjya – gandhādibhi(bhiḥ) naivedyaṃ (l.2) kṛtvā – dhvajadaṇḍapūjāṃ kuryāt – daṇḍāgre puṇyāhaṃ kṛtvā – sakalīkṛtya arghyaṃ sampādya । argyeṇa daṇḍa(ṇḍaṃ) saṃprokṣya kavacenāvakuṇṭhya (l.3) śaktyādiśaktiparyantaṃ yathākrameṇa saṃpūjya – oṅkārapūrvadaṇḍamūle brahmaṇe namaḥ । daṇḍamadhye viṣṇave namaḥ । ūrdhve rudrāya namaḥ । (l.4) tatvatraye ātmatatvatadadipatiśca saṃpūjya – skandayaṣṭhau brāhmami(mī)māheśvaryādisaptamātṝn saṃpūjya – upadaṇḍau daṇḍine namaḥ । (l.5) vāmapārśve – muṇḍine namaḥ । dārbhamālāṃ(lāyāṃ ) anantavāsukyādyaṣṭamahānāgān saṃpūjya ghaṇṭasadāśivāvalaye vāmādinavaśaktimabhyarcya - (p.76b, f71a, l.1) pīṭhadalāgreṣu । indrādilokapālān upadaleṣu ।
ukṣaṃ ca gopatiṃ caiva śaṅkukarṇaṃ tathaiva ca । 
ti(tī)kṣṇaśri(śṛ)ṅgaṃ tathā nandi*vṛṣaṃ ca paśupatistathā ॥ * (l.2)
mahodaro ....maścaiva sva sva nāmnaḥ prapūjayet ।
ghvajapaṭe vṛṣagāyatryā saṃpūjya – ityeṣā dadhimadhu(l.3)ghṛtasahitamudgānnaṃ nivedya dhūpadīpādibhiḥ saṃpūjya – sarvamaṅgalavādyaghoṣaiśca daṇḍavedikāyām anantā(l.4)dyaṣṭavidyeśvarān saṃpūjya upavedikāyāṃ vaikartanādi dvādaśādityān saṃpūjyā(jya) – ityeṣāṃ ghṛtagulapāyasānnāni ve(nive)dya (l.5) dhūpadīpau datvā saṃpūjya – dhyānam ।
ekaṃ ca pāṣadā? dvimukhaṃ ṣā...ṣaṇetraromālidarbhakarajjumālāḥ । 
cetāṅgarūpaṃ *dvibhujaṃ dvināsī ārūḍa(ḍha)padmāsanadaṇḍarūpam ॥ * (p.77a, l.1)
iti dhyātvā । ghṛtagulasahitaṃ pāyasānnaṃ nivedya – śaṅkhamaṅgalavādyaiḥ saṅghoṣadhvajapīṭhe (l.2) brahmendrādisthāneṣu lokapālanāmnaiḥ caturthyantena svāhāntabaliṃ dadyāt – evaṃ pratyahaṃ sāyaṃ prātaḥ itthaṃ kuryāt – utsaveśaṃ (l.3) sarvālaṅkā-rayuktanṛttagītādisahitagrāmapradakṣiṇaṃ kṛtvā – yatra yatra sandhidevānām āvāhanaṃ cet tatra tatra devasya dhūpa(l.4)dīpa-naivedyanṛttavādyādi kṛtvālayaṃ praviśya sthānamaṇṭape utsaveśasya naivedyādiṣoḍaśopacārāṃ(raṃ) kṛtvā evaṃ (l.5) sāyaṃ prātaḥ ॥
