mahātīrthasya pūrvasminmate (l.4) nityavat balibhramā(ma)ṇādyutsavānantaraṃ niśidhau? tīrthasaṃgrahaṇaṃ kāryaṃ rakṣāṃ pūrvavat kṛtvā āśiṣo vācaitvā maṇṭapa(l.5)madhye pūrvavat sthaṇḍilamekaṃ vidhāya । darbhai(rbhaiḥ) puṣpai(ṣpaiḥ) paristīrya । tanmadhye sarvālaṅkārasaṃyutaṃ manonmanikara(l.6)ku....(kumbhaṃ) sthāpya । tatparito gaṅgādyaṣṭakarakān(kalaśān?) saṃsthāpya – sakalīkaraṇaṃ ca kṛtvā । bhūtadaśuddhi(ddhya)ntaryāgaṃ kumbhe daṇḍabhaṅgi kṛtvā - (p.86a, l.1) gaurikalānyāsaṃ vidhāya bandhūbhāṇakāntāṃ? namāmi – gandhādisarvopacārai(raiḥ) saṃpūjya - (l.2) sarvāṣṭakarakeṣu gaṅgādidevyāḥ aṣṭau āvāhanādi-sarvopacārai(raiḥ) saṃpūjya – agnikāryaṃ pūrṇāntaṃ kṛtvā - āvāhana(l.3)krameṇa tattannāmani aṣṭottaraśataṃ hutvā – pūrṇāṃ hutvā – triśūlena saha kumbhān sarva(rvā)todyasamāyuktaṃ purādikaṃ prakṣa(dakṣa)ṇī(l.4)kṛtya – nadyāditīrthasthāneṣu snānārthaṃ saṃpraveśayediti saṅkalpya – puṇyāhaṃ kṛtvā – tīrthasya katukārthaṃ? (l.5) ekasmin karake gaṅgādyaṣṭatīrthān saṃpūjya tasminkaṇṭhe katukaṃ(kautukaṃ) badhvā tatkalaśajale nikṣipyālayaṃ praviśya tīrtha(l.6)saṃgrahaṇavidhiḥ ॥ (p.86b, f81a, l.1)
cūrṇotsavavidhiḥ –
	aparedyuḥ baliyānātparaṃ cūrṇotsavamārabhet – prāsādāgre sthaṇḍiladvaye rajanitailaghṛta(l.2)tāmbūlagandhapuṣpabhasma saṃsnāpya caturbhi(rbhiḥ) saṃskārai(raiḥ) saṃskṛtya ulūkhale pradhviṃ musale merum āsanamūrtiṃ (l.3) mūlamantrai(ntraiḥ) saṃpūjyā(jya) – rajanicūrṇaṃ droṇaṃ vā tadardhaṃ vā ulūkhale nikṣipya sahakoṣṭhaṃ ca nikṣipya – padmamālikhya (l.4) vināyakapūjādipuṇyāhaṃ kṛtvā – ekasmin śūlaṃ saṃsthāpya yājñi(jñī)yavṛkṣeṇa ulūkhalamusalaṃ ca salakṣaṇaṃ pare (l.5) saṃsthāpya vastreṇa saṃveṣṭya । lambakūrcaṃ dhṛtvā arghyavāriṇāstreṇa saṃprokṣya nirīkṣaṇādi catu(tuḥ)saṃskāraṃ kṛtvā (p.87a, l.1) tayormadhye sthaṇḍile rudrakumbhaṃ parito lokapālān(na)ṣṭau kalaśān saṃpūjya – ulu(lū)khalasya paritaḥ pūrvādidaleṣu dūrvā saha devi(vī)(l.2)...kā.... ca nikṣipya padamantreṇa vā bhaktastotreṇa vā drāviḍastotreṇa vā cūrṇīkṛtya tadagre agnikāryaṃ pūrṇāntaṃ kṛtvā । pañca(l.3)brahmaṣaḍaṅgaiśca samidājyena lājena yathāśakti hutvā – pūrṇāṃ kṛtvā tataḥ candrārka-vahnivasuvāsavasaptamātṝn (l.4) nandi.....bhrāgigajavaktraṣaḍānanāścā(śca) sarvāṇi vā ru(ṛ)ṣaya(yaḥ) saptakulā-calānā(nāṃ) sevanti sāmbaśivaparameśvarasya - (l.5).....rāyaṇasarasijāsanadevamukhyāḥ gandharvayakṣasurakinnarasindhabudhaḥ – vidyeśvarā(rāḥ) sakalarudragaṇādhipāśca – cūrṇanti (l.6) sevotsavanemaparameśvarasya - ॥ 2 ॥ lokāścaturdaśasamastadiśāśca jālā । māsāścaṣamātavayasakalātmajālāḥ (p.87b, f82a, l.1) cūrṇotsave parinaṭanti śivasya sevām । kurvanti muhupralayakalpayugāśca tārāḥ – nṛttagaṅgāditīrthasakalānimahādbhutāni vedādisarva-(l.2)nikhilāgamamantramukhyāḥ cūrṇotsave śivamahotsavapuṇyakāle sevanti siddhagaṇanāthamahātanubhāvāḥ ॥ 4 ॥
ākāśavāyusaliṃ? (l.3) caranti pra?dhi(di)vyabhūtaṃ śabdādisarvaviṣayāṇi manoharāṇi – cūrṇotsavārthamakhileśvarā pārvatīśasevāvinoda(l.4)māsaparimodayanti ॥ 5 ॥
	vi(vī)reśakālimadhusūdanavallabhāśca vāgīśvarī । nikhilayoginī yogapīṭhāḥ huṃ(l.5)....nti bhuvi bhairavadevatāśca cūrṇotsavapriya(yaṃ) haranti guṇā bhavanti ॥ 6 ॥
	pātālasaptaphaṇirājaśikhāmaṇināṃ (l.6) nīrājanāśca rajitā śivadeśikāśca cūrṇotsave sakalamantrajapena pūrṇām । śaivotsava(vaṃ) prakaṭayanti śivadvijendrāḥ ॥ 7 ॥ (p.88a, l.1)
	ityāmanandi ru(ṛ)ṣayaḥ pitṛdevatāścā(śca) vidyādharāśca catuṣṣaṣṭhikalā viśeṣaḥ puṇyā vayaṃ sakalakarmaphalādi-prāptā śivasya kṛpa(l.2)pārajanivasantaiḥ ॥ 8 ॥
	cūrṇotsavasya mahimānamihaiva vuktukoyaṃ lasamarthayadi(ti) cet punareva śambhoḥ no cet samasta(l.3)nirmāśca śivāgamāścā(śca) stotuṃ samarthayadi(ti) me pratibhāvayanti ॥ 9 ॥
	tataḥ svarṇādipātre cūrṇatailena miśrīkṛtya pañca(l.4)brahmaṣaḍaṅgai(ṅgaiḥ) mūlena saṃpūjya – dhūpadīpau datvā । sarva(rvā)-todyā(dya)samāyuktamālayaṃ pradakṣiṇīkṛtya – mūlaliṅge (l.5) śaktyādiśaktyantamabhyarcya – bhasmanāsaha brahmāṅgairdāpayitvā – kuṅkumoṣṇīṣaṃ ca dhṛtvā – tatpaṅkairālipya - tadgandha(l.6)puṣpādibhiralaṅkṛtya nivedya – dhūpadīpau datvā । sarveṣāṃ berāṇāṃ ca tatpaṅkairālipya । padmamudrāṃ pradarśya sa (p.88b, f83a, mahātīrthavidhiḥ, l.1) sarveṣāṃ berāṇāṃ dūrvāyā ghṛtaṃ śirasi nikṣipya – agni(gniṃ) visṛjya – tatkumbhajalairastraṃ saṃpūjya – dhūpadīpau datvā – svayaṃ ca (l.2) dhṛtvā sarveṣām uṣṇīṣārajani-tāmbūlādikaṃ datvā । triśūlena saha pu......dikaṃ pradakṣiṇi sarveṣāṃ dhṛtvā ālayaṃ praviśya iti (l.3) cūrṇotsavavidhiḥ ॥
(mahātīrthavidhiḥ -)
nadyā tīrtheṣu yathāsambhavaṃ tatti(ttī)re – prapādikaṃ kṛtvā paścāt pūrvavadaṅkuraṃ kṛtvā (l.4) tīrthasnānamācaret – sarveṣā-maspṛṣṭadoṣanivṛttyarthaṃ tīrthaprasādasidhyarthaṃ sarvadevapriyāvaha dharmādi(dī)n phalasiddhyarthaṃ (l.5) sālokādipadaprāptyarthaṃ ti(tī)rthatīre śaktyāsahāstrā(stra)rājasomāskandadyeṅkurachatracāmarādinā nānāvādyati(tī)rthakumbha(l.6)sahitaṃ prapādike devān saṃsthāpya tadagre sthaṇḍilamadhye manonmani gaṅgādyaṣṭakumbhāśca pūrvādisaṃsthāpyā(pya) pālikāśca (p.89a, l.1) saṃsthāpya । aśeṣataḥ saṃpūjya aiśānyāṃ durgāmāvāhyā(hya) । triśūlasannidhau aṣṭastriṃśatdevatāśchāṣṭādaśagaṇāśca lokapālā-nālāganaṃ (l.2) kṛtvā astrādidevatānāṃ kautukaṃ visṛjya tīrthamadhye visṛjya – pālikaiḥ saha śivādyastraparyantam । tatpaṭai(l.3)rabhiṣicya – sarvajanaiḥ saha snānamācaret – tataḥ ācāryaḥ tīrthakautukam udvāsyālayaṃ praviśya । sarveṣāṃ (l.4) devānāṃ sva sva kumbhamabhiṣicya naivedya dhūpadīpau datvālayaṃ praviśya – āsthānasthasarve brahmaghoṣasahitāḥ ācārya-(l.5)haste āśiṣya tairdatvā deśikaḥ āśiṣyakṣatairāśīrvādapurassaraṃ sarveṣāṃ brāhmaṇānāṃ dakṣiṇatāmbūlādi datvā – triśūlena saha snānaṃ kurvanti narottamaḥ sarvapāpai(paiḥ) pramucyate ni..............pannagāḥ itīhā(ha) tīrthavidhiḥ ॥ (p.89b, f89a, mahātīrthavidhiḥ, l.1)
atha ghaṭasnānam (ghaṭābhiṣeka) –
vidhi(vīdhī)harotsavasya pūrṇārthajanānāṃ sti(sthi)tikāraṇārthaṃ devaprā(pra)sādasiddhyarthaṃ indrādidevā(va)tā-sāmi(mī)pyasiddhyarthaṃ (l.2) ghaṭasnānaṃ kārayet – uṇḍe viśeṣeṇa homaṃ vidhāya pūrṇāṃ hutvā – tattadi(dī)śaṃ pradhāne kuṇḍe saṃyojya (l.3) śiva-mabhyarcya – pūrṇāṃ datvā – śivakumbhādi(dī)n viśeṣeṇābhyarcya – saṃpūjya agnisthadevān kumbhe saṃyojya – dhūpadīpau (l.4) datvā – ācāryādibhyo yathoktadakṣiṇā dadyāt – paricārakādibhyo vastrādidakṣiṇāṃ datvā kumbhānuddhṛtyālaya-pradakṣiṇaṃ (l.5) kṛtvā garbhagehe saṃsthāpya – mūlaliṅge ṣaḍadhvanyāsādīn nyastvābhiṣecayet vardhanīṃ pīṭhe vidyeśakalaśān (l.6) tattatsthāne'bhiṣicya – devīṃ śrīkaṇṭhanyāsaṃ pūrvavatkalaśe[ne?]nābhiṣicya dhūpadīpau mahāhavirnivedāyā(dya) । agni-sadanaṃ yāyāt । (p.90a, l.1) śivāgnau śirasā mūlenāghoreṇāṣṭottaraśataṃ hutvā pūrṇāṃ datvā – agniṃ yāgeśe saṃyojya – gurūpadiṣṭaprakāreṇa kumbha(l.2)vardhanyādipañcāvaraṇadevāśca tattatsthāne saṃyojya । tamapi visṛjya – prabhūtahaviṣaṃ dadet – biṃbiṃ(baṃ)prati snapanaṃ kārayediti (l.3) iti ghaṭābhiṣekavidhiḥ ॥
(avarohaṇavidhiḥ -)
	duṣṭanigrahaśiṣṭaparipālana(nā)rthaṃ ti(tī)rthadivasapūrvāhnādike । rātrau va brahmatāla(l.4)ghaṭapūrvamavarohaṇaṃ kuryādevormuttamottamaprakāreṇatridhvatsthaṃ vṛṣabhe saṃyojya - (l.5) vṛṣabhamapi śivāgre sthitavigrahe samāropya – āvaraṇa-devatāśca tadāvaraṇe saṃyojya – yathāvidhiṃ pūjayet - (l.6) taddine maunabali – homānte havirbha(rbhā)gaṃ devatāmityuktvā tannimityā maunabalimārabhet – ācāryaḥ somāskandaṃ (p.90b, l.1) snapanādipūjālaṅkṛtya – śaktyādiśaktyantaṃ saṃpūjya – daṇḍabhaṅgimuṇḍabhagniekatriṃśatkalānyāsaṃ śrīkaṇṭhanyāsaṃ ca kṛtvā dhyāyet – dakṣālāpi(l.2)tavāmaso.... guheśaṃ bhaje । iti sāṅgamāvaraṇapañcakopetam । saṃpūjya । vakṣyamāṇavat taddaivīṃ dhyātvābhyarcya - (l.3) jagataḥ śubhaṃ prārthya tasmāllabdhānujñe maunavratadharo baddhāñjalipuṭo jña(jñā)tvānnāṅgasamanvitam astrādidevān yāne (l.4) samāropya gandhādi-saṃyutatakhagekheṭakāstrādistu yuktabahurūpaṃ hṛdi smaranto maunavratadharavādyaghauṣatvināgrāsā (l.5) kukkuṭāṃ mātraṃ brahmasthānādi-sandhiṣu tattatsthāne vādyaghoṣasahitaṃ dhvajāvarohaṇapūrvaṃ balividhīya pūrvavat sandhidevān nyastvā (p.91a, l.1) krameṇa visṛjya pradakṣiṇīkṛtyālayaṃ praviśya – pūrvavanmantreṇa yathākrameṇā(ṇa) va(vā)ruhya pūrvasthale vinyasya । sarvānapi cānnaliṅgajale (l.2) visṛjayedityavarohaṇavidhiḥ ॥
(caṇḍotsavavidhiḥ -)
	dhvajārohaṇātpaścāt vṛṣabhe vṛṣabhaṃ nyaset – vṛṣabhasnapanaṃ kṛtvā gandhapuṣpādi(l.3)ryajet । mudga(dgā)nnaṃ ghṛtasaṃyuktaṃ kadalīphalasaṃyutam । naivaidyaṃ dāpayenmuktaḥ dhūpadīpādibhi(bhiḥ) saṃpūjya । (l.4) ṣoḍaśairupacārakai(kaiḥ) paścāt caṇḍamūrtiṃ yāgālaye samānīyya sthaṇḍile caṇḍakumbhaṃ sthāpya – saṃpūjya tatkumbha(l.5)jalenābhiṣicya । yāthāvi(vidhi) saṃpūjya । nirmālyādinā vibhūṣya agnikāryam – pūrṇāntaṃ hutvā samidānnājyai – brahmāṅgamantrai (l.6) pṛthak pṛthak aṣṭottaraśataṃ hutvā – caṇḍamūlena yathāśakti hutvā pūrṇāṃ datvā dravyānte vyāhṛtirhutvā tamapi tamapi visṛjya (p.91b, l.1) sarvamaṅgalopatam ālayapradakṣiṇaṃ kṛtvā tatsthāne niveśayediti caṇḍotsavavidhiḥ ॥
ācāryotsavavidhiḥ – (l.2)
ācāryaṃ gandhavastrakuṇḍalādyābharaṇādibhiralaṅkṛtya yathoktadakṣiṇāṃ ca pradāpayet – ācārya manasātri(tṛ)ptiṃ tasmāt tri(tṛ)ptiparaḥ (l.3) śivaḥ iti tamapi ru(ṛ)tvigbhiḥ saha śivavatsaṃpūjya । rathe śibikādau vā saṃsthāpya । nānāvādyai-(l.4)nṛ(rnṛ)ttagītādivedaghoṣaiścatracāmarairvividhadīpāssaha nṛpayajamānasarvajanaiśca puraṃ pradakṣiṇīkṛtya – yāne svagṛhaṃ praveśayet (l.5) paricārakajanādi yathoktadakṣiṇāṃ dadyāt – ityācāryotsavavidhiḥ ॥
(kalyāṇavratotsavam -)
daśame saptame pañcame vāhni vivāha(p.92a, l.1)vidhivadaupacārakeṇa kalyāṇavratotsavaṃ kārayet ।
(devyotsavam -)
atha devyotsavaṃ navāhasaptāhapañcāhatriyāhamekāhaṃ vā utsavaṃ kārayet – (l.2) ekādaśadivasarātrāvindrā(ndra)vimānādisarvaṃ mantraṃ kṛtya – saṃprokṣya – snapanapūrvaṃ devamabhiṣicyālaṅkṛtya – tanmadhye vimānastha(l.3)śivamānīyā(ya) taṃ devīpūrvacaṇḍeśāntaṃ bhūpayajamānavādyaiḥ saha pradakṣiṇatrayaṃ kārayitvā ālayapraveśakāle (l.4) gopurāgre vindhyāgre va(vā) praṇayanakalahaṃ vyapohya – vino(nā/noda)darśanaṃ ca kārayitvā yathāvidhi praveśayediti (l.5) devyotsavavidhiḥ ॥
(utsavavivaraṇam -)
āsthānamaṇṭapāgre vā prāsādasyāgrake'pi vā – gomayālepanaṃ kṛtvā sthaṇḍiladvitayaṃ kuru । (l.6) darbhai(rbhaiḥ) puṣpai(ṣpaiḥ) paristīryā(rya) sthaṇḍilaṃ kūrcayeddhṛdā – sthaṇḍiladvidayaṃ cettu śūlameva tri vinyaset – tadagre sthāpayet (p.92b, l.1) bherīṃ puṇyāhaṃ vācayettataḥ astrabherīṃ ca saṃpūjya – bherīṃ santāṭa(ḍa)yet budhaḥ । tadyath – atha guru(ruḥ) atha guru(ruḥ) (rep.?) snānādikaṃ kṛtvā (l.2) saumyāsyopaviśya । saṅkalpya – asyāṃ śubhatithau । śrīmatparameśvarasya navadinadhvajārohaṇa-kalyāṇāsevārthaṃ sakaladevatā(l.3)vāhanārthaṃ samastanaramṛgapaśupakṣiṇāṃ kṣemārogyavijayasiddhyarthaṃ bherītāḍanaṃ kariṣye – puṇyāhajalena (l.4) ..........saṃprokṣya – sakalīkṛtya – sāmānyārghyeṇāstreṇa triśūlaṃ saṃprokṣya – kavacenābhyukṣya astrāsanāya (l.5) huṃ phaṇṇamaḥ । astramūrtaye huṃphaṇṇamaḥ – astreśaṃ ṣaḍutthāsanaṃ saṃpūjya । o hām astrāya huṃ phaṇṇamaḥ ityāvāhyā(hya) (l.6) tri(stha)ṇḍiladevatān nyaset – madhyapatre – oṃ hāṃ rudrāya namaḥ । dakṣiṇapatre – brahmaṇe namaḥ । vāmapatre – viṣṇave namaḥ । pālikā(p.93a, l.1)madhye – oṃ devyai namaḥ । pālikādakṣiṇe sarasvatyai namaḥ । pālikā-vāmapārśve mahālakṣmyai namaḥ । kumbhāgro(gre) gaṇapataye namaḥ । (l.2) kumbhamadhye skandāya namaḥ । daṇḍāgre śāstre namaḥ । daṇḍamadhye bhāskarāya namaḥ । daṇḍakamale candrāya namaḥ । daṇḍamūle caṇḍāya sanamaḥ । (l.3) pūrvādidalāgreṣu indrāya namaḥ । mātre namaḥ । vīrabhadrāya namaḥ । durgāyai namaḥ । kṣetrapālāya namaḥ । vasave namaḥ । gaṇebhyo namaḥ । (l.4) nakṣatrebhyo namaḥ । ityastreśaṃ pūjitakrameṇa gandhapuṣpadhūpadīpanaivedyatāmbūlaṃ datvā ācamanārghyaṃ datvā - (l.5) tataḥ bherīpūjāṃ kuryāt । kasalīkṛtya sāmānyārghyeṇa bheri(rīṃ) saṃprokṣya praṇavāsanaṃ datvā bherīṃ navavastreṇāścā(cchā)dya (l.6) gandhādibhirabhyarcya bherīmadhye dakṣiṇavāmabhāge devau iti vacanāt bherīmadhye śambhave namaḥ । dakṣiṇe viṣṇave namaḥ । vāme brahmaṇe (p.93b, l.1) namaḥ । kileṣu brāhmyai namaḥ । māheśvaryai namaḥ । kaumāryai namaḥ । vaiṣṇavyai namaḥ । vārāhyai namaḥ । māhendriyai namaḥ । (l.2) cāmuṇ